# Test: ze config fmt prints a block's children in YANG definition order
#
# QUESTION: does the shipped `ze config fmt`, over the full set of YANG modules
# the binary registers, print each block's children where the YANG declares
# them, an augmented child after the block's own, and is its output already
# formatted? The unit tests build the order over fixture modules and the config
# test binary's modules; only the binary carries every plugin's augment, and
# only the command reads and writes the file the operator owns.
#
# The input is written in name order, the order the printer used before.
# Definition order, read from the YANG:
#   bgp: router-id, then session, then peer (ze-bgp-conf.yang, container bgp);
#     by name: peer, router-id, session.
#   bgp peer: connection, session, then filter (grouping peer-fields), then
#     rpki, which ze-rpki.yang adds by augment "/bgp:bgp/bgp:peer";
#     by name: connection, filter, rpki, session.
#   system: host, then domain (ze-system-conf.yang); by name: domain, host.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-config-yang-definition-order AC-1 (children in definition
#   order through the command), the augment row of D-1 (rpki after the peer's
#   own children, although it sorts before session), AC-9 (fmt of fmt changes
#   no byte: --check after -w).
# PREVENTS: the YANG-to-schema converter ordering a block's children by name,
#   and a format that a second run changes again.
tmpfs=order.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer zulu {
		connection {
			local {
				ip 192.0.2.1
			}
			remote {
				ip 192.0.2.26
			}
		}
		filter {
			import {
				final accept
			}
			export {
				final accept
			}
		}
		rpki {
			action {
				invalid reject
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				remote 65026
			}
		}
	}
	router-id 10.0.0.1
	session {
		asn {
			local 65000
		}
	}
}
system {
	domain example.net
	host edge1
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config fmt order.conf:exit=0
expect=stdout:pattern=(?s)\n\trouter-id 10\.0\.0\.1\n\tsession \{\n.*\n\tpeer zulu \{\n
expect=stdout:pattern=(?s)\n\t\tconnection \{\n.*\n\t\tsession \{\n.*\n\t\tfilter \{\n.*\n\t\trpki \{\n
expect=stdout:pattern=(?s)\n\thost edge1\n\tdomain example\.net\n

# AC-9: the written file is a fixed point of the formatter.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config fmt -w order.conf:exit=0
expect=stderr:contains=Formatted: order.conf

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze config fmt --check order.conf:exit=0

cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze config fmt order.conf:exit=0
expect=stdout:pattern=(?s)\n\trouter-id 10\.0\.0\.1\n\tsession \{\n.*\n\tpeer zulu \{\n
expect=stdout:pattern=(?s)\n\thost edge1\n\tdomain example\.net\n
